I am currently preparing for an ascension run with a Caveman who is
unfortunately very far from ready for it. I am playing wishless/
genoless, as I have for my previous 10 or so ascensions, but this time
around the RNG has been pretty unkind.  I have explored the entire
dungeon and found zero magic markers and one scroll of enchant armor,
resulting in a very poorly equipped Caveman.  So, before I make a run
at the Wizard I was wondering if anybody with experience ascending
marginal characters has any advice.  I have made runs with characters
who had lowish hp and bad AC but they were normally equipped with a
good arsenal of spells and items.  My Caveman has no spells and no
range-weapon capabilities.  Here is a brief overview of some key stats/
inventory:

-level 24 400 hp (only real upside)
-13 ac (boots ofspeed, +1SDSM, a useless burnt robe, non-magical
shield and helmet, gauntlets of power, jumping boots in BoH)
-all relevant rings, 1 amulet of life-saving, +6 scepter o might (only
available source ofMR)
- 3 wands of death, 2 wands of cancellation,4 wands of teleport plus 2
scrolls of charging, not to mention the 2 very useless wands of
wishing I am carrying around for no good reason
-scrolls of gold detection and crystal balls for the planes

 I think that my wands of death and teleport may be able to carry me
through, but I could easily run into tough spots with the WIzard and
the planes ahead of me.  If I ever get surrounded by a lot of tough
monsters my AC will not allow me to hold up.  Fortunately I am lawful
so Solars will not be a problem at least.  Thank you for any input you
might have.



